  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Challenging stigma and discrimination to improve access to and quality of HIV services in the Caribbean - Americas - Multicountry Americas CVC-COIN (01-Oct-2016-30-Sep-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Americas CVC-COIN, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Jamaica)This program has the following goals: To reduce the spread and impact of HIV in key populations across the Caribbean. The objectives of this program are: Community systems and key population networks use effective advocacy to obtain social accountability mechanisms and scale-up best practice interventions by national programs..  Health and community workers deliver stigma and discrimination-free services to key populations, improving access to and retention in care..  Improved legal and policy environments support delivery of and access to health and justice services for key populations.</narrative>
  </description>
